WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Our first guest is
the director of the

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
National Institute of
Allergy and Infectious Disease

00:00:03.336 --> 00:00:05.939 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the chief medical advise
to the president.

00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:07.874 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome to the show
Dr. Anthony Fauci.

00:00:07.874 --> 00:00:10.377 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here, Doctor.

00:00:10.377 --> 00:00:12.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
Thank you for having me.

00:00:12.178 --> 00:00:15.382 size:88% position:44%
-Your office looks about
the way I expect it --

00:00:15.382 --> 00:00:16.016 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
a lot of books.

00:00:16.016 --> 00:00:18.685 size:84% position:42%
Maybe a new addition is
the bobblehead there.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:19.819 line:92%
I'm assuming that was a gift

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:22.055 size:88% position:44%
and you didn't have to
buy your own bobblehead?

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:24.691 line:92%
-That's true. It was a gift.

00:00:24.691 --> 00:00:28.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
-How do you -- Do you feel lik
they did a good job

00:00:28.328 --> 00:00:30.296 line:92%
depicting you in the bobblehead?

00:00:30.296 --> 00:00:31.831 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Well, yeah, I guess so.

00:00:31.831 --> 00:00:34.534 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, we're so immersed
in what we're doing,

00:00:34.534 --> 00:00:36.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't pay
that much attention to it,

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:37.771 line:92%
but it looks pretty good.

00:00:37.771 --> 00:00:40.140 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I guess I'd be pretty upset
if you were sending notes

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:42.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
back and forth to
the bobblehead people.

00:00:42.409 --> 00:00:43.877 line:92%
-Yeah, that wouldn't be good

00:00:43.877 --> 00:00:47.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, I have to ask --
it strikes me that the questio

00:00:47.847 --> 00:00:49.182 align:start size:94% position:6%
that you probably get
asked the most

00:00:49.182 --> 00:00:50.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
that maybe is
a little hard to answer

00:00:50.917 --> 00:00:52.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
and maybe you don't like
having to answer is

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:55.722 align:start size:94% position:6%
people asking, "When are thing
going to back to normal?"

00:00:55.722 --> 00:00:59.125 align:start size:94% position:6%
How do you respond when
you're asked that question now

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:00.493 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, you know,
you really can't give

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:03.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
a definitive answer
at all because there are

00:01:03.463 --> 00:01:05.265 line:92%
so many moving parts to this

00:01:05.265 --> 00:01:07.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
There are so many
things in play.

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:10.003 align:start size:94% position:6%
We can say,
if you look at the fact

00:01:10.003 --> 00:01:13.373 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we now have three
and soon to be more

00:01:13.373 --> 00:01:17.143 align:start size:94% position:6%
highly efficacious vaccines,
that we really do see

00:01:17.143 --> 00:01:18.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
the light at the end
of the tunnel.

00:01:18.878 --> 00:01:20.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean,
we still have the challeng

00:01:20.713 --> 00:01:23.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we went way, way, way u
in a bad winter

00:01:23.983 --> 00:01:25.752 size:88% position:44%
and then we started to
come down precipitously.

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:31.157
But we are plateauing now at
around 50,000 cases a day.

00:01:31.157 --> 00:01:32.792 line:92%
We can't declare victory now

00:01:32.792 --> 00:01:34.461 align:start size:94% position:6%
That would really be
ill-advised,

00:01:34.461 --> 00:01:37.263 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we see
what happened in Europe.

00:01:37.263 --> 00:01:37.931 size:88% position:44% line:92%
They did the same thing.

00:01:37.931 --> 00:01:41.234 align:start size:94% position:6%
They're generally
three to four weeks ahead of u

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.735 line:92%
in the dynamics of the outbreak.

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:45.138 align:start size:94% position:6%
They went up,
started to come down.

00:01:45.138 --> 00:01:45.705 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
They plateaued.

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:48.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
They pulled back on
the public-health measures

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.243 line:92%
and now they are rebounding.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:52.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
We desperately have to
avoid that.

00:01:52.178 --> 00:01:54.314 line:92%
If we just keep pushing along,

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:58.051
vaccinating 2 million to
3 million people per day,

00:01:58.051 --> 00:01:58.718 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
keep a lid on it,

00:01:58.718 --> 00:02:01.121 align:start size:94% position:6%
keep the
public-health measures going

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:02.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we're going to be
in good shape.

00:02:02.188 --> 00:02:06.226 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think as the months go by --
April, May, June, July --

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:09.195 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think we're going to continu
to do better and better.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:10.330 line:92%
When you say "normal," Seth,

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:11.431 line:92%
I'm not sure what you mean

00:02:11.431 --> 00:02:15.268
It's not going to be exactly the
way it was before this happened,

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:17.370 size:81% position:41%
but it's going to be
a heck of a lot better

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:20.673 align:start size:94% position:6%
as we approach the
late spring, early summer

00:02:20.673 --> 00:02:21.441 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and get into the fall.

00:02:21.441 --> 00:02:24.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would say it was approaching
a degree of normality

00:02:24.677 --> 00:02:27.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
as we get into the
late summer and early fall

00:02:27.881 --> 00:02:29.716 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We talk about
public-health measures.

00:02:29.716 --> 00:02:32.485 align:start size:94% position:6%
Of course,
that means things like masks

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:34.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is your response --
You must pass people

00:02:34.654 --> 00:02:38.458
in the street or in public
that are not wearing masks

00:02:38.458 --> 00:02:39.225 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Do you say something?

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:41.995 align:start size:94% position:6%
Do they get
a dirty look from you?

00:02:41.995 --> 00:02:43.963 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You know,
I don't do that, Seth,

00:02:43.963 --> 00:02:46.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
because that, in some respects
would sort of be

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:49.235 line:92%
futile to do that just get int

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.570 line:92%
that kind of a hostile exchange.

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:52.805 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it really is
disturbing to me,

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.975 align:start size:94% position:6%
because I've been through
all of these phases

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:57.810 align:start size:94% position:6%
that we have been through,
like when we tried to

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:01.948
open up the economy last summer,
and then, all of a sudden,

00:03:01.948 --> 00:03:03.917 align:start size:94% position:6%
everybody pulled back
on everything

00:03:03.917 --> 00:03:05.919 line:92%
and we had this big surge.

00:03:05.919 --> 00:03:07.520 size:84% position:42% line:92%
We know what happens --

00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:09.789 align:start size:94% position:6%
First of all,
we understand the need

00:03:09.789 --> 00:03:12.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
and the feeling that you
really want to get back normal

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:15.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
You want to put
these things behind you.

00:03:15.228 --> 00:03:16.529 line:92%
But if you do it prematurely

00:03:16.529 --> 00:03:17.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's going to come back
to bite you.

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:22.101 align:start size:94% position:6%
We've seen that happen
multiple times in this country

00:03:22.101 --> 00:03:24.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it's going on
right now in Europe.

00:03:24.237 --> 00:03:27.340 align:start size:94% position:6%
So we've just got to
hang in there a bit longer

00:03:27.340 --> 00:03:28.041 size:78% position:39% line:92%
This is going do end.

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:29.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
We're not going to be
this way forever.

00:03:29.776 --> 00:03:34.214
But if we pull back prematurely,
we're going to get into trouble.

00:03:34.214 --> 00:03:35.882 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Obviously, one of
the problems here is,

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:39.219
a virus does not appreciat
what we've all gone throug

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:40.653 line:92%
and the sacrifices we've made.

00:03:40.653 --> 00:03:42.789
I think sometimes,
that's the way, as human beings,

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:45.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
we react to news that things
might get worse again.

00:03:45.892 --> 00:03:50.763
Variants strikes me as something
that when we heard about it,

00:03:50.763 --> 00:03:52.465 align:start size:94% position:6%
again, it's very natural
to think,

00:03:52.465 --> 00:03:54.167 align:start size:94% position:6%
"I can't believe
there's something else."

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:56.236 align:start size:94% position:6%
But could you speak to
the seriousness

00:03:56.236 --> 00:03:58.771 align:start size:94% position:6%
and maybe explain to peopl
who don't understand

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:00.840 line:92%
exactly what variants are.

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:04.811 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, variants are
mutational changes in the viru

00:04:04.811 --> 00:04:06.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
that make it
a little bit different.

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:09.749 align:start size:94% position:6%
Sometimes, it changes
the function of the virus,

00:04:09.749 --> 00:04:11.884 line:92%
makes it more easy to transmit

00:04:11.884 --> 00:04:14.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
sometimes makes
it even more serious

00:04:14.621 --> 00:04:17.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you get infected,
regardless of the illness.

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:19.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
The thing that
we worry about the most --

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:24.163
that it will essentially evade
the protection of the vaccine.

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:28.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
Right now, there's one variant
that originated in the U.K

00:04:28.501 --> 00:04:32.305 size:78% position:39%
They're given numbers
that people generally

00:04:32.305 --> 00:04:33.339 line:92%
don't need to understand.

00:04:33.339 --> 00:04:35.341 size:84% position:42% line:92%
This one is called 117.

00:04:35.341 --> 00:04:39.345
It's starting to become dominant
in the United States.

00:04:39.345 --> 00:04:40.780 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Fortunately for us,

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:44.617 align:start size:94% position:6%
our vaccines seem to
protect pretty well against it

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:48.221
There's another variant that
originated in South Africa

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:50.657 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a version of which
is in Brazil

00:04:50.657 --> 00:04:52.859 align:start size:94% position:6%
that's a little bit
more problematic,

00:04:52.859 --> 00:04:54.661 line:92%
which means that the antibodie

00:04:54.661 --> 00:04:56.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the vaccines that
we all get --

00:04:56.562 --> 00:05:00.700 align:start size:94% position:6%
those antibodies are diminishe
in their efficacy

00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:03.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
when they confront
this particular variant,

00:05:03.403 --> 00:05:06.105 align:start size:94% position:6%
so which means that
the efficacy of the vaccin

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:08.508 align:start size:94% position:6%
might diminish a bit,
which means we might have to

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:12.011 align:start size:94% position:6%
boost people either with
the original vaccine

00:05:12.011 --> 00:05:14.013 align:start size:94% position:6%
or with a version of
the new vaccine.

00:05:14.013 --> 00:05:15.548 align:start size:94% position:6%
We don't have to do
that yet, Seth,

00:05:15.548 --> 00:05:19.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we may not have to do that
but you got to prepared,

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:22.388 size:88% position:44%
because you have to take
the variant seriously.

00:05:22.388 --> 00:05:24.557 size:78% position:39%
I don't think they're
showstoppers for us.

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:27.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don't think they're going to
just diminish greatly

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:30.263
what we're doing, but we have to
pay attention to it.

00:05:30.263 --> 00:05:31.898 line:92%
-When a new variant turns up

00:05:31.898 --> 00:05:33.533 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you ever say
to one of your colleagues,

00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:36.836 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Could one of you
tell people this has happened?

00:05:36.836 --> 00:05:37.870 line:92%
Because I feel like I've given

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.806 align:start size:94% position:6%
so much bad news
over the last year.

00:05:39.806 --> 00:05:41.874 size:84% position:42%
I would love it to come
from somebody else."

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:45.044 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, you know, occasionally,
I feel that way,

00:05:45.044 --> 00:05:47.714
but that's not going to be
in the cards for what I do

00:05:47.714 --> 00:05:48.514 line:92%
I have to be out there wit

00:05:48.514 --> 00:05:51.751
the good news
and the bad news, unfortunately.

00:05:51.751 --> 00:05:53.553 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You testified before
Congress today --

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:55.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
not for first time,
but for the first time

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:56.756 line:92%
under the Biden administration

00:05:56.756 --> 00:05:59.025 align:start size:94% position:6%
Did it feel
any different for you?

00:05:59.025 --> 00:06:01.260 line:92%
-No, it was about the same

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:06.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, it was -- When you get
these kinds of hearings,

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:09.769 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the most part,
they ask good questions abou

00:06:09.769 --> 00:06:10.970 line:92%
things that they want to know.

00:06:10.970 --> 00:06:13.272 align:start size:94% position:6%
Occasionally,
depending upon the party,

00:06:13.272 --> 00:06:17.677
somebody will get snippy and
want you to answer a question.

00:06:17.677 --> 00:06:19.078 line:92%
Like today, somebody said,

00:06:19.078 --> 00:06:20.446 align:start size:94% position:6%
"A 'yes' or 'no'
answer to this,"

00:06:20.446 --> 00:06:22.615 align:start size:94% position:6%
when there was no
"yes" or "no" answer.

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:24.550 align:start size:94% position:6%
"But we want
a 'yes' or 'no' answer."

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:25.918 line:92%
So, you know, you sort of

00:06:25.918 --> 00:06:29.689 size:78% position:39%
play around with that
and circumvent it.

00:06:29.689 --> 00:06:31.290 line:92%
-I'm sure you're getting good at

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:33.092 align:start size:94% position:6%
that part of
the job, unfortunately.

00:06:33.092 --> 00:06:34.127 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hey, we're going to be
right back.

00:06:34.127 --> 00:06:37.764
I have a few more questions with
Dr. Anthony Fauci.

